<title>USA: Starter sees Q4 sales above 1995 Q4 sales.</title>
<headline>Starter sees Q4 sales above 1995 Q4 sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW HAVEN, Conn. 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Starter Corp said on Thursday that its current inventory puts it in position to meet anticipated demand in the fourth quarter, which should lead to higher sales compared with the fourth quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>The company reported close to $80 million in net sales for the 1995 fourth quarter.</p>
<p>On Thursday the company reported third quarter net sales of $170.5 million and earnings of $0.40 per share.</p>
</text>
